    "type": "mc",
    "prompt": "Aline writes a correct calculation. Then she covers two digits which are the same with a sticker (see the picture: 4□ + 5□ = 104). Which digit is under the stickers?",
    "image": "qimages/kangaroo/ca-2013-g0304/q02.webp",
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "2"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "4"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "5"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "7"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "8"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "D",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Tens first",
        "body": "The tens give $40 + 50 = 90$. The two hidden digits must make up the rest: $104 - 90 = 14$. Two equal digits adding to 14 are $7 + 7$.\n\nCheck: $47 + 57 = 104$. ✓\n\n**Answer: (D) 7**"
      },
      {
        "title": "Try the choices",
        "body": "- 2: $42 + 52 = 94$\n- 4: $44 + 54 = 98$\n- 5: $45 + 55 = 100$\n- 7: $47 + 57 = 104$ ✓\n\n**Answer: (D) 7**"
      }
    ],
