        "text": "4"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "5"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "6"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "D",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Family by family",
        "body": "Each family with twins has 2 boys, so at most 1 girl. The third family can have 3 girls. At most $1 + 1 + 3 = 5$ girls.\n\n**Answer: (D) 5**"
      },
      {
        "title": "Count the boys",
        "body": "There are 9 children. At least 4 of them are boys (two pairs of twins). So at most $9 - 4 = 5$ girls, and 5 is possible.\n\n**Answer: (D) 5**"
      }
    ],
