    "prompt": "John is 33 years old. His three sons are 5, 6 and 10 years old. In how many years will the three sons together be as old as their father?",
    "image": null,
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "4"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "6"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "8"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "10"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "12"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "B",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Close the gap",
        "body": "Now the sons together are $5 + 6 + 10 = 21$, which is $33 - 21 = 12$ years less than John. Every year the sons together get 3 years older and John only 1, so the gap shrinks by 2 each year. $12 \\div 2 = 6$ years.\n\n**Answer: (B) 6**"
      },
      {
        "title": "Check",
        "body": "In 6 years: John is 39, the sons are 11, 12 and 16: $11 + 12 + 16 = 39$. ✓\n\n**Answer: (B) 6**"
      }
    ],
