      {
        "title": "Add all three facts",
        "body": "- peaches + apricots = 18\n- oranges + apricots = 28\n- oranges + peaches = 30 (the fruits that are not apricots)\n\nAdding them counts every fruit twice: $18 + 28 + 30 = 76$, so there are $76 \\div 2 = 38$ fruits.\n\n**Answer: (D) 38**"
      },
      {
        "title": "Find each kind",
        "body": "Oranges + peaches = 30 and oranges + apricots = 28, so peaches are 2 more than apricots. Peaches + apricots = 18 gives 10 peaches and 8 apricots. Then oranges $= 30 - 10 = 20$. Total $20 + 8 + 10 = 38$.\n\n**Answer: (D) 38**"
      }
